  <static seed="36" source="Library/PCC/BasicAlgebra/Exponents/exponentsMultiplication0.pg">
    <statement><p>Use the properties of exponents to simplify the following</p>
<p><m>{t^{20}}\cdot{t^{13}} =</m>
<fillin characters="12" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>t^{33}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>We <em>add</em> the exponents as follows</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}
           t^{20}\cdot t^{13}\amp =t^{20+13}\\
                             \amp =t^{33}
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
</solution>
